## 🧠 Quick Revision Cheat Sheet

| Topic | Key Thing to Remember |
|-------|-----------------------|
| Variables | No type declaration needed. `type()` to check. |
| Strings | **Immutable** — can't change individual characters. |
| `input()` | Always returns **string**. Cast with `int()`, `float()`. |
| Lists | **Mutable**, use `[]`, supports all operations. |
| Tuples | **Immutable**, use `()`, faster than lists. |
| Single tuple | Must have comma: `(5,)` not `(5)`. |
| Dicts | Key-value pairs, keys must be unique & immutable. |
| `=` assignment | Lists: creates **reference**, not copy. Use `.copy()`. |
| `==` vs `is` | `==` checks value, `is` checks identity (memory). |
| Slicing | `[start:stop:step]`, stop is **exclusive**. |
| `[::-1]` | Reverses any sequence. |
| `*args` | Collects extra positional args as **tuple**. |
| `**kwargs` | Collects extra keyword args as **dictionary**. |
| File `"w"` | **Overwrites** existing content! |
| File `"a"` | **Appends** to end. |
| `with open()` | Auto-closes file. Always prefer this. |
| `enumerate()` | Gives `(index, value)` pairs. |
| `%` in Python | Always non-negative result (unlike C/Java). |

---

> **Good luck with your test! 🍀** Focus on understanding *why* things work, not just memorizing syntax.
